{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PLAN CERTIFIED after five review rounds. Recording what each round found, because every one named\nsomething real and three of the five were MY errors — an implementer should trust this plan's\nspecifics rather than re-deriving them, and should know why they are worded so precisely.\n\nROUND 1-2 (the parametrization premise): the plan said DC convergence tests would be 'parametrized\nalongside Cloud's where the mechanism is shared'. IMPOSSIBLE. Cloud's suites hardcode Cloud-only\ninternals — comment_limits.truncate_comment_body (test_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py:154)\nand ADF_PATH / _ADF_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT=32000 (test_outbound_description_length_convergence.py:31-34)\n— which have no DC equivalent. Following it literally would have meant restructuring\nincident-hardened Cloud tests, which this epic's own AC forbids. Now: SEPARATE DC files, the\ndefault rather than a fallback.\n\nROUND 3 (the injection seam): a DC comment convergence test driven through\ncompute_outbound_mutations CANNOT reach DC's sanitizer. That function (outbound_differ.py:382-391)\ntakes outbound_mapper/inbound_mapper/links but NO sanitizer, and line 744 calls _diff_comments\nWITHOUT forwarding one, so _resolve_sanitizer(None) -> select_backend(load_config()).sanitizer =\nCLOUD. The test would have converged against Cloud's truncation while reporting DC convergence.\nFixed with no production change: _diff_comments already accepts sanitizer= (outbound_comments.py:167,\nthe ticket-21ca seam).\n\nROUND 4 — TWO FINDINGS, AND THE SECOND CAUGHT ME WRITING A TEST THAT CANNOT FAIL:\n (a) The OR-GUARD. outbound_differ.py:431 is\n     'if outbound_mapper is None or inbound_mapper is None or links is None:' — so injecting ONLY\n     outbound_mapper still fires the fallback and lets it resolve all three from config. All THREE\n     must be injected. I had read that exact line in an earlier round and missed the implication.\n (b) MY 'DISCRIMINATING ASSERTION' WAS VACUOUS. I had required the comment test to assert DC's\n     length boundary and truncation suffix to prove it used DC's path. But DC's\n     WikiTextCodec.fit_outbound and Cloud's comment_limits.truncate_comment_body truncate at the\n     SAME 32767 limit and append a BYTE-IDENTICAL suffix — ' … [truncated by reconciler]' at\n     rich_text.py:69 and comment_limits.py:46 — and compute 'keep' the same way. So that assertion\n     passes under EITHER sanitizer: precisely the tests-that-cannot-fail defect sibling ticket 2944\n     exists to delete, which I introduced while enforcing a rule against it. The comment test now\n     requires an IDENTITY/RECORDING proof that the injected DC sanitizer actually ran, and its\n     mutation check targets the INJECTION rather than the value. The DESCRIPTION test keeps a\n     value-based discriminator, which IS legitimate there because DC fits plain chars at 32767\n     while Cloud fits ADF-SERIALIZED size at 32000 — those genuinely differ.\n\nROUND 5 (stale metadata): the file_impact I had declared still listed Cloud's EXISTING convergence\nfiles with the reason 'extend Cloud coverage to DC' — contradicting the rewritten plan that says\nthose files stay BYTE-UNCHANGED. LESSON WORTH CARRYING: file_impact is REVIEWED MATERIAL, so the\n'grep the whole document after editing' sweep must cover it too, not just the prose. Corrected to\nthe two NEW DC files plus the provenance-comment-only change to backend.py.\n\nALSO NOTE, from the earlier research comment: the comment CEILING itself is settled (32767 is the\ndocumented default of jira.text.field.character.limit, which covers Comments as well as Description\n— jpm.xml, JRASERVER-28519). Do NOT re-measure it and do NOT mark it UNVERIFIED; cite the\nprovenance at the binding. That it is admin-configurable is a separate ticket, 049e-9fac-a821-4ea2."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785707040728485001,"uuid":"82d4ed8d-bf23-4d7a-9377-72668ce00742"}